### Please describe the problem in your own words.

`git annex testremote --test-readonly <file> <remote>` and also the non-readonly variant recently started to fail in the Forgejo-aneksajo test suite after NeuroDebian's update to 10.20261026. This is the error I am seeing:

```
2026-10-31T13:26:29.6800139Z Remote Tests
2026-10-31T13:26:29.6802324Z   unavailable remote
2026-10-31T13:26:29.9914722Z     removeKey:                                       FAIL (0.31s)
2026-10-31T13:26:29.9922352Z       ./Command/TestRemote.hs:463:
2026-10-31T13:26:29.9930303Z       (got: Right ())
2026-10-31T13:26:29.9930672Z       Use -p '/unavailable remote.removeKey/' to rerun this test only.
2026-10-31T13:26:30.0465183Z     storeKey:                                        FAIL (0.05s)
2026-10-31T13:26:30.0467492Z       ./Command/TestRemote.hs:463:
2026-10-31T13:26:30.0467710Z       (got: Right ())
2026-10-31T13:26:30.0468003Z       Use -p '/unavailable remote.storeKey/' to rerun this test only.
2026-10-31T13:26:30.0663456Z     checkPresent:                                    FAIL (0.01s)
2026-10-31T13:26:30.0665582Z       ./Command/TestRemote.hs:463:
2026-10-31T13:26:30.0665808Z       (got: Right True)
2026-10-31T13:26:30.0667078Z       Use -p '/checkPresent/' to rerun this test only.
```
(the rest show "OK", `3 out of 35 tests failed (0.53s)`)

After testing different versions I found that `10.20260901.post1` still worked and `10.20261020` installed from PyPI exhibits the error. There is another version `10.20261005` in between that doesn't have a package in PyPI so I couldn't easily test. Since it mentions changes on testremote it seems likely the issue started there.

I also see the issue with a local clone and p2phttp, see reproducer.


### What steps will reproduce the problem?

To setup a to-be-cloned repo and start p2phttp:

[[!format bash """
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euxo pipefail

mkdir repo
cd repo
git init
git annex init
echo test > test.txt
git annex add test.txt
git commit -m commit
git annex p2phttp --bind 127.0.0.1 --port 54321 -J2 --debug --wideopen
"""]]

To clone and run testremote:

[[!format bash """
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euxo pipefail

git clone repo repo-clone
cd repo-clone
git config annex.security.allowed-ip-addresses 127.0.0.1
git config remote.origin.annexUrl annex+http://127.0.0.1:54321
git annex get test.txt
git annex testremote --test-readonly test.txt origin
"""]]


### What version of git-annex are you using? On what operating system?

Multiple, the issue is present in 10.20261020 and later, it is not present in 10.20260901 and before.


