Additionally I've tested this against a public repository hosted on <https://atris.fz-juelich.de> and get a somewhat different error:

[[!format sh """
$ git annex testremote --test-readonly outputs/ccm/nhsat-nino34-e10.pdf origin
Remote Tests
  unavailable remote
    removeKey:                                       git-credential-oauth 0.15.1
input: map[host:atris.fz-juelich.de:443 path:git-annex-p2phttp protocol:annex+https wwwauth[]:Basic realm="Gitea"]
Please complete authentication in your browser...
annex+https://atris.fz-juelich.de:443/login/oauth/authorize?client_id=a4792ccc-144e-407e-86c9-5e7d8d9c3269&code_challenge=RZz-MkOeyBMB3dn3es9-ytpsG-IKhPKkY0p7-hq1rA8&code_challenge_method=S256&redirect_uri=http%3A%2F%2F127.0.0.1%3A34579&response_type=code&state=5cIyb0zY-zVUjYjRWngHTDJXAdLoUdhjAPcBqBVDzcU
Unable to open browser using 'xdg-open': exit status 4
"""]]

To me it looks like it is not replacing the remote url with a proper unavailable one for these tests, leading to the ATRIS case breaking on git-credential-oauth and the local case breaking because the operations finish successfully when they shouldn't.

### Have you had any luck using git-annex before? (Sometimes we get tired of reading bug reports all day and a lil' positive end note does wonders)


